      "dayNumber": 1,
      "originalText": "dhritarashtra uvacha: dharma-kshetre kuru-kshetre...",
      "translatedText": "On the sacred field of Kurukshetra, assembled and eager for battle, what did my sons and the sons of Pandu do?",
      "sourceReference": "Bhagavad Gita 1.1",
      "tags": "dharma,duty,battlefield,beginning"
    },
    {
      "id": 1002,
      "categoryId": 101,
      "dayNumber": 2,
      "originalText": "na tv evaham jatu nasam...",
      "translatedText": "Never was there a time when I did not exist, nor you, nor all these kings; nor in the future shall any of us cease to be.",
      "sourceReference": "Bhagavad Gita 2.12",
      "tags": "soul,eternity,existence"
    },
    {
      "id": 1003,
      "categoryId": 101,
      "dayNumber": 3,
      "originalText": "na jayate mriyate va kadachin...",
      "translatedText": "The soul is neither born, and nor does it die; nor having once existed, does it ever cease to be.",
      "sourceReference": "Bhagavad Gita 2.20",
      "tags": "soul,immortality"
    },
    {
      "id": 1004,
      "categoryId": 101,
      "dayNumber": 4,
      "originalText": "karmany evadhikaras te...",
      "translatedText": "You have a right to perform your prescribed duties, but you are not entitled to the fruits of your actions.",
      "sourceReference": "Bhagavad Gita 2.47",
      "tags": "duty,karma,detachment"
    },
    {
      "id": 1005,
      "categoryId": 101,
      "dayNumber": 5,
      "originalText": "yogah karmasu kaushalam...",
      "translatedText": "Yoga is skill in action — performing one's duty with an even mind, undisturbed by success or failure.",
      "sourceReference": "Bhagavad Gita 2.50",
      "tags": "yoga,balance,action"
    }
